                    ]
                  }
                },
                "type": "object"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Per-bar value labels. `false`/absent (default) → none. `true` → each bar's\n`close` value with the chart's numeric formatter. Object → `format(value)`\nand/or a `position` override. Default position is above the bar. Labels are\n`aria-hidden` — the values already live in the accessible ChartDataList."
          },
          "height": {
            "type": "number"
          },
          "hoverKey": {
            "description": "CONTROLLED synchronised hover key (FR-3). A bar's key is its `label` (the\ndate/category). When provided (string or null), the crosshair + tooltip track\nthis key instead of the chart's internal pointer hover (null ⇒ nothing shown),\nletting a parent share one hover channel across several aligned charts. Absent\n(`undefined`) keeps the legacy uncontrolled behaviour.",
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          },
          "keyboardNav": {
            "description": "FR-5 — keyboard navigation of the data points (roving tabindex). When `true`\n(or implied by wiring `onSelectKey`), a thin focusable overlay is rendered\nover the bars: the chart owns ONE tab stop, ←/↑/→/↓ move the focus between\nbars (data order), Home/End jump to the first/last, Enter/Space select the\nfocused bar (`onSelectKey`), Escape leaves the navigation. Each focused bar\nannounces its `label` + O/H/L/C. Absent ⇒ no overlay, rendering unchanged.",
            "type": "boolean"
